WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.125 --> 00:00:02.044
Hey guys, it's Logan Marmino,

00:00:02.127 --> 00:00:05.839
and did you know this show
is actually based on real-life Josh?

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:07.424
-Oh, hey!
-Hey.

00:00:07.508 --> 00:00:09.384
Do we have time
to walk around set and talk?

00:00:09.468 --> 00:00:10.093
Yeah, let's do it.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.641
So, this is where
the Dubin family home schools.

00:00:16.266 --> 00:00:17.935
We can tell your desk because
look how serious it is

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:18.852
compared to the other ones.

00:00:19.186 --> 00:00:21.396
Did you have this home school room?

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:22.940
No, we didn't have this home school room.

00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:25.025
We did like home school,
like, in our bedroom.

00:00:25.108 --> 00:00:29.029
I did it in my closet, under my clothes,
doing my school at my desk.

00:00:29.279 --> 00:00:30.989
-And, hit!
-Woah!

00:00:32.533 --> 00:00:34.993
How much of the series is "real" real?

00:00:35.077 --> 00:00:40.582
I think every episode has a piece of my life
that's real, and it really--

00:00:40.666 --> 00:00:43.418
-Did you memorize everybody's--
-I really memorized everyone's names.

00:00:43.502 --> 00:00:45.629
I used to, like, I really got a copy
of the eighth-grade yearbook.

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:46.213
Yeah.

00:00:46.296 --> 00:00:47.506
'Cause I was actually
going into high school.

00:00:47.589 --> 00:00:48.674
I memorized everyone's name.

00:00:48.757 --> 00:00:49.591
And just like that scene,

00:00:49.675 --> 00:00:51.844
where you were walking down the hallway
saying "hi" to everyone.

00:00:51.927 --> 00:00:53.345
It's like, I did exactly that.

00:00:53.428 --> 00:00:56.098
Hey! Dave Conrad, Josh Dubin.

00:00:56.181 --> 00:00:58.600
Good to meet you. Love that haircut.

00:00:58.684 --> 00:01:00.352
So one thing I find
people always want to know

00:01:00.435 --> 00:01:02.104
is how we found you.

00:01:02.187 --> 00:01:03.355
And we found you
in a pretty cool way.

00:01:03.438 --> 00:01:05.232
-So, I made a post on Instagram.
-And... yes.

00:01:05.315 --> 00:01:09.862
"Hey, we're looking for an amputee
to portray a boy about 12 years old."

00:01:09.945 --> 00:01:12.990
Yeah, some person tagged me
on the Instagram post,

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:15.158
and you guys contacted me.

00:01:15.242 --> 00:01:17.578
It was so wild,
because you've never acted before.

00:01:17.661 --> 00:01:21.498
Yeah, I've had no acting experience,
in school, in anything.

00:01:21.582 --> 00:01:22.708
There's a lot of actors in Los Angeles,

00:01:22.791 --> 00:01:25.752
but there's not that many people, like,
your age with one leg who wanna act.

00:01:25.836 --> 00:01:27.337
Actually, there's basically none.

00:01:27.421 --> 00:01:28.797
Because we would've found them easily.

00:01:28.881 --> 00:01:29.631
-Yes.
-Right?

00:01:29.715 --> 00:01:33.510
It was really important to us
to find someone who actually has one leg

00:01:33.594 --> 00:01:35.012
to play a person with one leg.

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:37.347
Then we were so glad to find you.

00:01:38.265 --> 00:01:42.102
We're gonna show you some of the Easter eggs
that are hidden around the set.

00:01:42.186 --> 00:01:44.938
My brother, Luke, who works
with baby sea turtles, is represented.

00:01:45.022 --> 00:01:47.399
There's like eight or ten
sea turtles all around here.

00:01:47.482 --> 00:01:48.442
Sea turtle...

00:01:48.525 --> 00:01:49.359
sea turtle...

00:01:49.443 --> 00:01:50.277
another sea turtle.

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:53.113
This was my
great-great-grandfather's chair.

00:01:53.197 --> 00:01:57.409
Literally, like, my grandfather was rocked
in this exact rocking chair.

00:01:57.492 --> 00:01:59.119
-Which is pretty wild.
-That is cool.

00:01:59.203 --> 00:02:01.079
My parents just shipped it
across the country,

00:02:01.163 --> 00:02:02.247
and now here it is on our set.

00:02:02.623 --> 00:02:05.959
I used it when you all were babies,
and I would rock you all.

00:02:06.043 --> 00:02:07.711
-It didn't feel small to you?
-No.

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:11.840
So these are all photos
of you in real life

00:02:11.924 --> 00:02:14.176
-and the other actors that play...
-And all the other actors, yes.

00:02:14.259 --> 00:02:16.428
-That's Romy and her actual brothers.
-Yeah.

00:02:16.512 --> 00:02:18.597
But it looks like the family.

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:19.765
-Yeah, totally.
-That's why it worked.

00:02:19.848 --> 00:02:21.350
-Do you know who drew that drawing?
-Who?

00:02:21.433 --> 00:02:22.351
-Me!
-You did?

00:02:22.434 --> 00:02:23.936
Yeah, I was like six or seven.

00:02:24.019 --> 00:02:26.396
-Ah, that's pretty cool.
-Yeah.

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:28.190
Do we wanna go see the middle school now?

00:02:28.273 --> 00:02:30.234
-Yeah, let's show the middle school.
-Let's go see the middle school.

00:02:31.443 --> 00:02:34.196
We just walked out the house,
which is like ten feet,

00:02:34.279 --> 00:02:35.656
and now we're already at the school.

00:02:37.491 --> 00:02:39.368
So this is the foyer of the school.

00:02:39.451 --> 00:02:41.286
A lot of big scenes happen
right in this room.

00:02:41.537 --> 00:02:42.996
I'm so excited.

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:44.957
In my real life,
I did way too many activities.

00:02:45.332 --> 00:02:46.708
In the show, we needed to figure out,

00:02:46.792 --> 00:02:49.336
like, how can we show
Josh doing so many things?

00:02:49.419 --> 00:02:50.921
And so we constructed this board.

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:52.214
What do we have on some of these things?

00:02:52.297 --> 00:02:54.258
-Josh Sundquist.
-Oh, my real name!

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:55.843
Did you sign that?

00:02:55.926 --> 00:02:57.386
-No, I did not.
-That's not my handwriting.

00:02:57.803 --> 00:03:00.013
So we have Soccer Club, which I did.

00:03:00.097 --> 00:03:03.350
Chess Club, Writer's Club,
Hockey Club, Cheer Club, Robot Club.

00:03:03.433 --> 00:03:06.812
What were some clubs that you did,
or hobbies and sports?

00:03:06.895 --> 00:03:08.689
Actually, I wrestled.

00:03:08.772 --> 00:03:09.773
-Did I ever tell you that?
-Oh, no.

00:03:09.857 --> 00:03:12.234
Yeah, I was on the varsity wrestling team
my first year of school.

00:03:12.317 --> 00:03:16.655
I was terrible, but that was kind of how
we got the idea of the soccer episode.

00:03:16.738 --> 00:03:18.907
It was kinda like my experience
as being on the wrestling team,

00:03:18.991 --> 00:03:20.450
and are people going to go easy on me...

00:03:20.534 --> 00:03:22.578
-Oh, okay.
-or not when they wrestle with me.

00:03:22.661 --> 00:03:24.162
We wanted Josh to play soccer,
'cause I played--

00:03:24.246 --> 00:03:27.624
And like second-guessed all of his life,
like getting on teams...

00:03:27.708 --> 00:03:29.418
-Exactly, it's like people go
-and if he was really good--

00:03:29.501 --> 00:03:30.335
easy on you, right.

00:03:30.586 --> 00:03:34.923
What if all of my coaches have lied to me
and pretended that I was better than I am

00:03:35.007 --> 00:03:36.717
because my mom made them.

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:38.844
How can I know how good I am at soccer?

00:03:39.094 --> 00:03:43.807
When I was your age, I never saw someone
who looked like me on screen.

00:03:43.891 --> 00:03:45.100
-Do you feel that way?
-Oh, yeah.

00:03:45.184 --> 00:03:46.560
-Right? You've never seen that.
-Never.

00:03:46.643 --> 00:03:48.645
And so to be able
to do a show like this...

00:03:49.146 --> 00:03:51.190
And it's not,
"Oh, that's the kid with the leg."

00:03:51.273 --> 00:03:53.275
-It's, "Oh, he's like me."
-Yes.

00:03:53.358 --> 00:03:55.652
And they can see,
on television, the normal life

00:03:55.736 --> 00:03:58.530
-of a middle-schooler with a prosthetic.
-Yes, totally.

00:03:58.614 --> 00:04:00.574
That lightning is pretty sweet, dude.

00:04:00.657 --> 00:04:01.742
Yeah, I love it.

00:04:01.825 --> 00:04:03.827
It makes you look like a superhero.

00:04:04.745 --> 00:04:08.207
Tell us about how you rehearse lines,
'cause I think this is so cool.

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:09.625
-With Peyton and Trinity?
-Yeah.

00:04:10.042 --> 00:04:13.587
So, every night we rehearse lines,
go to sleep, wake up,

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:15.506
-and then they're all in our heads.
-Yeah.

00:04:15.589 --> 00:04:16.465
We have it down to a science.

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:20.010
Have you and Peyton and Trinity
all become friends in real life?

00:04:20.093 --> 00:04:21.595
Oh, definitely, yeah.

00:04:21.803 --> 00:04:23.222
This has been really fun,
walking around the set,

00:04:23.305 --> 00:04:25.224
finding the Easter eggs together
and talking about it.

00:04:25.307 --> 00:04:27.643
But you have to go to a costume fitting.

00:04:27.726 --> 00:04:29.353
-For the Halloween episode.
-Right.

00:04:29.436 --> 00:04:30.437
-Gotta do it.
-All right.

00:04:30.521 --> 00:04:31.605
Let's head out.

00:04:35.192 --> 00:04:36.985
And cut. Great, got it.

